              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چمن زدن (chaman zadan) — \"to mow the lawn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "همسایه ما هر هفته چمن میزند. hamsâye-ye mâ har hafte chaman mizanad. Our neighbour mows the lawn every week."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chaman 'lawn, grass' + zadan 'to strike'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chaman is the Persian word for a lawn; EtymDB lists it beside chamidan, 'to stroll' (EtymDB), but its origin is not settled. zadan, 'to strike', is inherited."
            }
          ]
        },
