              "text": "دورهمی (dowrehami) — \"a get-together (of family or friends)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آخر هفته ها در خانه مادربزرگ دورهمی داریم. âkhar-e haftehâ dar khâne-ye mâdarbozorg dowrehami dârim. At weekends we have a get-together at grandmother's house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Colloquial: dowr-e ham 'around each other' + -i."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dowrehami is built in Persian on dowr, 'circle, round', a loan usually traced to Arabic dawr, and native ham, 'together', with -i: sitting round together. EtymDB has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
